    {
      "id": "hybrid::n4",
      "kind": "fuse",
      "label": "Reciprocal rank fusion",
      "parent_ids": [
        "hybrid::n2",
        "hybrid::n3"
      ],
      "duration_ms": 0.0,
      "explain": "RRF combines two independently-ranked lists without needing to normalize their raw score scales, since it only uses each result's rank position (1 / (RRF_K + rank)) \u2014 this is why a keyword-exact BM25 hit and a semantically-close dense hit can be merged fairly, and why a chunk found by only one branch still earns a nonzero fused score instead of being dropped.",
